-- Test Description
-- This test ensures the GEM in TBI mode deals with runt frames properly.
-- 
-- Functional coverage
-- · Ensures that in TBI mode that received frames that are less than 64 bytes
--   plus extension are discarded.
--
-- Detailed Test Description
--
-- 1. Setup DMA wait states for the test.
-- 2. Initialise the GEM for TBI 32-bit DMA mode.
-- 3. Enable all interrupts, and then enable receive.
--
-- 4. Enable copy all frames.
-- 5. Receive a frame that is 15 bytes long. (Should be discarded)
-- 6. Receive a frame that is 13 bytes long. (Should be discarded)
-- 7. Receive a frame that is 4 bytes long. (Should be discarded)
-- 8. Receive a frame that is 3 bytes long. (Should be discarded)
-- 9. Receive a valid minimum length frame which is copied to memory
--10. Check statistic registers and ensure above operation was handled 
--    properly.
--
--11. Disable copy all frames.
--12. Receive a frame with 6 bytes of preamble. (Should be discarded)
--13. Receive a frame with 6 bytes of preamble, and SFD. (Should be discarded)
--14. Receive a frame with 6 bytes of preamble, SFD, and the MAC destination 
--    address. (Should be discarded)
--15. Receive a frame with 6 bytes of preamble, SFD, the MAC destination 
--    address and an arbitrary source address. (Should be discarded)
--16. Receive a valid minimum length frame which is copied to memory
--17. Check statistic registers and ensure above operation was handled 
--    properly.
--
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- *****************************************************************************
-- 1. Setup DMA wait states for the test.
-- *****************************************************************************
wait_states 0
bus_grant_delay 0

pinsc(50) loopback 0 half_duplex 1  extint 0 speed 0 --  check reset state

-- *****************************************************************************
-- 2. Initialise the GEM for 100Mbits/s 32-bit DMA mode.
-- 3. Enable all interrupts, and then enable receive.
-- 4. Enable copy all frames.
-- *****************************************************************************
